  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PreComm 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'The lab team is choosing which cancer drug ideas to move into animal
    testing. They meet with your advocacy group to learn what outcomes matter most
    to patients.


    <b>In this situation, what impact do community advocates have
    on preclinical research?</b>'
  explanation: Community advocates help research teams understand what matters most
    to patients, such as quality of life, access, and side effects. Their input can
    guide which ideas move forward so research stays patient-centered from the start.
  correctAnswer: Helping researchers prioritize projects that reflect patient needs
    and values
  incorrectAnswer1: Helping researchers decide which drug idea is the safest to test
  incorrectAnswer2: Helping researchers get approval to move forward with animal
    studies quicker
  incorrectAnswer3: Helping researchers design new laboratory experiments
  questionRole: Community Advocate
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: PreClinical
